# ScriptableObjects (Project Config)

Prefer ScriptableObjects for **all** tunable game-design and project settings. The user balances from assets, not by digging in code.

## What belongs in an SO

- Combat: damage, RPM, spread, recoil, reload time, ammo
- Player: move/sprint speed, jump, ground check, acceleration
- Camera: sensitivity, FOV, ADS multipliers
- Project/feature flags and shared defaults that designers may tweak

## What stays on the MonoBehaviour

- Scene references (CharacterController, camera transform, muzzle)
- Runtime state (current ammo, cooldown timers, isGrounded)
- Wiring: which config asset this instance uses

## Conventions

```
Assets/Data/
  Player/PlayerMotorConfig.asset
  Weapons/RifleConfig.asset
  Camera/LookConfig.asset
```

- Type name ends with `Config` (or `Settings` for project-wide): `WeaponConfig`, `PlayerMotorConfig`
- One concern per SO type; create new assets for variants (Pistol vs Rifle), not subclasses unless behavior differs
- Fields: clear names, `[Min(0)]` / ranges where useful, `[Tooltip]` in Russian only if it helps designers — code comments stay Russian for non-obvious why
- Default assets created and assigned on prefabs/scenes by the agent — do not leave null config refs

## Usage pattern

```csharp
[SerializeField] WeaponConfig _config;

void Fire() {
  // значения баланса только из конфига
  var damage = _config.Damage;
}
```

- Do not duplicate the same tunable as both SO field and local serialized float
- Shared constants that are never balanced can stay as `const` / static readonly in code
